- No `gemini` resource and no `crewcut-dataset` resource in `ht-resource list` (checked by steward and executor). Consequences: describe step, continuity judge (shot correspondence) and all Gemini spend are "not run"; comparison with d509bed is "not run" unless the dataset is obtainable another way (e.g. Hugging Face `Jack-Jieke-Wu/crewcut` revision d509bed over heng-network — the owner of the comparison, task-maker, decides whether that stands as the published dataset; recorded, not a protocol change). No substitute model may stand in for the judge or descriptions.

## Judge setting (from scorer, steward#8)
- `crewcut/scoring/judge.py:51` uses max_tokens=3; Gemini models via the world's gemini resource returned empty content (finish_reason=length). Documents fix neither the judge model (I3 待定事项 2; `CREWCUT_JUDGE_*` "chosen per benchmark version") nor a way to make thinking models answer within 3 tokens. Whether to change the setting or choose a judge model that works is the maintainer's. Until decided, shot correspondence (and anything depending on it) is "not run", without conclusion. No position changes the code or the setting.
